    "geometry": "313 authored cuboid parts and 20 bones, including two fixed inner rail frames, eight individual missiles and two separate faceted outer rapid pods. Visible Hellfire body/nose/bands/nozzle/fins use the source mesh length and fin envelope. Texture remains an authored 1024 atlas.",
    "launch": "Actual Hellfire spawn uses fixed rail center transformed by body yaw/bank. Player initial heading is body-forward despite off-axis sight aim. AI launch yaw is zero in body space with pitch toward the observed target; source hover body-alignment gate remains authoritative.",
    "permissions": "Observation and friendly/occlusion permission ray follows the actual observed target. Fixed-launch guided flight has its own real collision trajectory. No source-angle change bypasses existing hurt, PvP, crew or block checks.",
    "ammunition": "Current player eight-round total alternates left/right then advances through four rails. Render visibility follows synchronized Rockets. NBT ammunition restoration preserves the next rail. AI uses source infinite ammunition and leaves all modeled rounds visible; source automatic visual rack reload behavior is not established.",
    "flightVisual": "Flying Hellfire rod length and fin width/height corrected; trailing particle attachment moves to half the actual visible length. Tracking, damage, source flight coefficients and smoke/fire activation delays are unchanged.",
    "wreck": "Wreck posing resets part visibility and includes detached outer pods and eight missile model fragments. These are visual fragments, not live secondary ordnance."
  },
  "adaptationsAndUnknowns": [
    "One authored transport airframe remains a Minecraft adaptation; standard gunship / Blackhawk variants and their absolute skeleton transforms are not fully reproduced.",
    "Outer pod 19-port face tessellation and faceting are authored approximations. The original mesh topology / tube count was not decoded here; 19 is not claimed as a source fact.",
    "Current player 240 gun / 8 Hellfire stores and manual 60-tick cooldown remain adaptations. Source marine gunship Hellfire clipCapacity 4, other variants differ; whether each of two weapon entries owns that capacity or shares it remains unresolved.",
    "Source D_M1 launcher locator duplicates D_M3 position, while physical missile0..3 joints are distinct. This checkpoint uses physical model joints; exact emitter selection and reload/visibility behavior remain unresolved.",
    "Source locator pitch about 4.5 degrees is recorded but current authored racks are level; AI launch pitch follows the weapon profile. Exact source model pose versus projectile emission transform needs further engine investigation.",
    "Rapid unguided weapon firing, player input allocation, original capacities, staged effect flags Unknown1, complete movement/action bank and source audio/FX identities remain open.",
    "No original executable run or copied original mesh/texture. Native validation cannot establish exact original-engine behavior or dedicated multiplayer correctness. Full creatures, soldiers, vehicle items and sound goal remains active."
  ]
